{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/lem-generator-choice","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:generator-choice","kind":"lemma","title":"Generator choice in the division algorithm","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-groebner-basis","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-division-algorithm"],"proofs":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/prf-generator-choice"],"tags":["groebner-basis","division","generator"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.UnitalGroebner.generator_choice","text":"generator-choice-lemma.md","leanSource":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/generator-choice-lemma.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:generator-choice\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> be a commutative ring with unity, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-algebra which\nis free as an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(B, &#x3C;)</code> an\n<a href=\"#def:admissible-system\">admissible system</a>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code> be a\ntwo-sided ideal of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> generated by a unital\n<a href=\"#def:groebner-basis\">Gröbner--Shirshov basis</a>\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G = \\{g_\\gamma \\mid \\gamma \\in \\Gamma\\}</code>.</p>\n<p>Then in the <a href=\"#def:division-algorithm\">division algorithm</a>, we may\nchoose <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h_i \\in I</code> so that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h_i = g_{\\gamma_i}</code> for some\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma_i \\in \\Gamma</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/generator-choice-lemma.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Lemma","number":"2.4.1"}
